    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "NQ0NQ",
      "x": -1044,
      "y": 758,
      "width": 856,
      "height": 10950,
      "content": "Yep. Since you’re owning frontend/design, I’d make the PRD hackathon-scoped, with a very explicit MVP so the team doesn’t accidentally build Expedia + Pokémon Go + Instagram before lunch. 😅\nPRD: Journey\nWorking concept: Multiplayer travel game\nTheme: Travel: The journey, not the destination\nStatus: Hackathon MVP\n1. Product vision\nTurn travelling together into a multiplayer game.\nFriends join a trip together. During the journey, each player receives personalised missions based on their preferences, location and trip context.\nPlayers complete missions, take photos, earn points and unlock passport stamps/badges.\nAt the end, the trip becomes a shared memory artifact showing what happened, who did what and the moments collected along the way.\n2. Core experience\nCREATE ACCOUNT\n      ↓\nSET TRAVEL PERSONALITY\n      ↓\nCREATE / JOIN TRIP\n      ↓\nFRIENDS JOIN\n      ↓\nSTART JOURNEY\n      ↓\nAI GENERATES MISSIONS\n      ↓\nPLAY WHILE TRAVELLING\n      ↓\nCOMPLETE MISSIONS\n   ↙        ↓       ↘\nPHOTO     GPS      MANUAL\n   ↘        ↓       ↙\n     POINTS + BADGES\n           ↓\n        ARRIVE\n           ↓\n    JOURNEY RECAP\n           ↓\n   DIGITAL PASSPORT\n3. User profile\nEach player has a lightweight account.\nProfile\nName\nAvatar\nTravel preferences\nPlay preferences\nPassport\nPrevious trips\nBadges / achievements\nTravel personality\nKeep onboarding playful rather than making users fill in a settings form.\nWhat are you into?\n🍜 Food\n📸 Photography\n🌲 Nature\n🎵 Music\n🏛 Culture\n🛍 Shopping\n🤪 Weird stuff\n🏃 Active\n🎮 Games\n🧭 Exploring\nThen:\nHow adventurous are you?\nChill ●━━━━━━ Wild\nAI uses these signals when generating missions.\n4. Trips & groups\nTrips are temporary multiplayer rooms.\nCreate trip\nCreator enters:\nTrip name\nStarting point\nDestination\nApproximate duration\nTransport type\nExample:\n🚗 Namibia Road Trip\nCape Town → Windhoek\n4 players · ~15 hours\nJoin trip\nFriends join through:\nInvite link\nQR code\nShort trip code\nFor hackathon scope, trip code is probably enough.\n5. Trip lobby\nThis should feel like the moment before starting a multiplayer game.\nNAMIBIA ROAD TRIP\n4/6 players ready\n🟢 Jackie\n🟢 Amy\n🟢 Florian\n🟡 Sam\nEveryone ready?\nSTART JOURNEY\nBehind the scenes, AI now has:\nplayer preferences + group composition + journey information\nand generates the game.\n6. Mission system\nThis is the core product.\nThere are three mission types.\n👤 Personal missions\nOnly assigned to one player.\nFOOD HUNTER\nFind the weirdest snack at the next stop.\n📸 Photo required\n+150 XP\nAI should bias these toward that player's interests.\n🤫 Secret missions\nOther players don't know your objective.\nSECRET MISSION\nConvince someone else to suggest stopping without directly asking them.\n+300 XP\nThese create interaction between players.\n🧑‍🤝‍🧑 Group missions\nEveryone participates.\n📸 ALBUM COVER\nRecreate the worst band photo possible at your next stop.\nEveryone must appear.\n+500 GROUP XP\nThese should be less frequent and feel more significant.\n7. Contextual missions\nGPS makes the game respond to the actual journey.\nPotential signals:\nCurrent location\nDistance travelled\nSpeed\nTime\nStops\nRoute deviation\nNearby landmarks\nJourney progress\nExample:\n🌅 GOLDEN HOUR\nSunset is approaching.\nTake a group photo before the sun disappears.\n+400 XP\nOr:\n🌀 DETOUR\nYou've left the planned route.\nFind something interesting before returning.\n+250 XP\nFor the hackathon, you could fake/simplify most contextual intelligence. GPS location + elapsed time + AI is enough to demonstrate the idea.\n8. Completing missions\nKeep this extremely simple.\nMission card →\nCOMPLETE\nThen choose:\n📸 Take photo\nor\n✓ Mark complete\nPhoto gets stored with:\nmission\nplayer\ntimestamp\nGPS location\ntrip\nThat metadata becomes useful later.\n9. Points\nPoints provide immediate feedback.\nIndividual XP\nCompleting missions increases personal score.\nJackie\n1,450 XP\nGroup XP\nGroup missions contribute toward a shared score.\n🚗 Namibia Crew\n4,850 XP\nDon't overbuild the scoring system for the hackathon.\nMission completed → points.\nDone.\n10. Passport & badges 🛂\nThe long-term collectible layer.\nEach user's profile contains their Travel Passport.\nInstead of country stamps, it records how they travel.\nExamples:\n🌅 Dawn Patrol\nStarted a journey before sunrise\n🌀 Lost & Loving It\nCompleted a mission while off-route\n🚗 Road Warrior\nTravelled 1,000km\n🤝 Travel Buddy\nCompleted 5 trips with the same person\n📸 Documentarian\nCompleted 25 photo missions\nSome badges can have rarity:\nCommon · Rare · Epic · Legendary\nThat gives the product a collectible-game feeling without requiring a huge system.\n11. End-of-trip artifact\nThis should be one of the hero experiences.\nWhen GPS detects arrival, or the host ends the journey:\n🏁 JOURNEY COMPLETE\nCape Town → Windhoek\n15h 42m\n1,478 km\n4 travellers\n23 missions\n18 photos\n7 badges\nThen generate a Journey Story.\nCrew awards\n🧭 Jackie\nExplorer\n🍟 Amy\nSnack Commander\n😴 Sam\nProfessional Passenger\nTimeline\n08:02\n🚗 Journey started\n\n09:14\n📸 Jackie completed \"First Sighting\"\n\n11:42\n🍔 Group completed \"Mystery Snack\"\n\n13:06\n🏅 Road Warrior unlocked\n\n15:22\n🌀 Unexpected detour\n\n18:43\n🌅 Group completed \"Golden Hour\"\n\n23:44\n🏁 Arrived\nPhotos are woven through the timeline.\nIdeally AI also generates a tiny playful summary:\nFour friends left Cape Town. One questionable pie, three wrong turns and 1,478km later, they somehow made it.\nThis becomes something users can save/share/revisit.\n12. Frontend architecture\nFor your part, I'd think of it as six main surfaces:\nSurfaceKey UI\nOnboarding\npreferences + travel personality\nHome\npassport + create/join trip\nLobby\nplayers + ready state\nJourney ⭐\nmissions + progress + map\nMission\nchallenge + photo/complete\nRecap ⭐\nmemories + stats + awards\nI'd spend most of your design time on Journey and Recap.\nThose are the screens that sell the concept.\n13. Journey screen\nI wouldn't make the map the hero.\nSomething closer to:\n┌─────────────────────────────┐\n│ 🚗 NAMIBIA ROAD TRIP        │\n│ 284km travelled       4 👥  │\n│                             │\n│ ───────────●──────────────  │\n│ Cape Town          Windhoek │\n│                             │\n│ YOUR MISSION                │\n│                             │\n│ ┌─────────────────────────┐ │\n│ │ 🍟 FOOD HUNTER          │ │\n│ │                         │ │\n│ │ Find the weirdest snack │ │\n│ │ at your next stop.      │ │\n│ │                         │ │\n│ │ +150 XP                 │ │\n│ │                         │ │\n│ │       OPEN MISSION →    │ │\n│ └─────────────────────────┘ │\n│                             │\n│ 🔒 Secret mission waiting   │\n│                             │\n│ ─────────────────────────── │\n│ 🗺️ Journey  🛂 Passport 👤 │\n└─────────────────────────────┘\nThe feeling should be game HUD layered onto real travel, rather than navigation software.\n14. Technical architecture\nYour proposed stack maps cleanly:\nSupabase\nAccounts\nProfiles/preferences\nTrips\nTrip members\nMissions\nMission completion\nPoints\nBadges\nPhotos / storage\n↓\nAI API\nInputs:\ntrip + player + preferences + location/context\nOutputs structured mission JSON:\n{\n  \"title\": \"Snack Hunter\",\n  \"description\": \"Find the strangest snack at your next stop.\",\n  \"type\": \"personal\",\n  \"verification\": \"photo\",\n  \"points\": 150\n}\n↓\nMapbox / GPS\nLocation\nJourney progress\nNearby context\nDistance\nStops\n↓\nVercel\nFrontend\nServer/API routes\nAI orchestration\n15. Hackathon MVP 🔨\nI'd aggressively cut scope.\nMust work\nCreate profile + choose interests\nCreate trip\nFriends join trip\nStart journey\nAI generates personalised missions\nMission feed\nComplete mission\nUpload photo\nEarn points\nEnd trip\nGenerate journey recap\nFake / simplify\nGPS triggers\nComplex achievements\nLive route tracking\nAI photo verification\nLeaderboards\nBadge progression\nNearby business integrations\nDynamic detours\nYou can show those in the pitch as where this goes next.\nThe demo story\nThis matters more than having 40 features.\nFour friends are driving somewhere.\nThey join the trip.\nAI learns that Jackie likes photography, Amy likes food and Sam likes music.\nStart Journey.\nJackie gets:\n📸 Photograph something that looks like an album cover.\nAmy gets:\n🍟 Find the strangest road-trip snack.\nSam secretly gets:\n🤫 Get everyone singing the same song.\nThey complete them.\nPhotos appear.\nPoints accumulate.\nThen:\nEND JOURNEY →\n✨ Their journey transforms into the finished memory artifact.\nThat final transformation is your demo payoff.\nThe pitch becomes very simple:\nWe usually remember where we travelled. Journey helps us remember what happened along the way."
    },
